From b74a66cd65050328f60fb62cc7f34981e8bdfeb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sagar Bussa <sagar.bussa@morsemicro.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Apr 2017 12:45:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: mlme s1g ecsa support

Update the STA-side MLME to consider short beacons in channel switch
time calculations, which effectively considers the time based on DTIM
beacon intervals, as ECSA IE is advertised in DTIM beacons.

This patch is S1G specific and can have an impact on ECSA functionality
of other Wi-Fi radios, which delays channel switch operation based on
DTIM interval.
---
 net/mac80211/mlme.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/net/mac80211/mlme.c b/net/mac80211/mlme.c
index 88751b0eb317a..d45cd644a5609 100644
--- a/net/mac80211/mlme.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mlme.c
@@ -2607,6 +2607,7 @@ ieee80211_sta_process_chanswitch(struct ieee80211_link_data *link,
 	now = jiffies;
 	link->u.mgd.csa.time = now +
 			       TU_TO_JIFFIES((max_t(int, csa_ie.count, 1) - 1) *
+					     sdata->vif.bss_conf.dtim_period *
 					     link->conf->beacon_int);
 
 	if (ieee80211_vif_link_active(&sdata->vif, link->link_id) &&
